[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4066552782","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116513#issuecomment-4066552782","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116513","id":4066552782,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7yYqvO","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-16T10:10:05Z","updated_at":"2026-03-16T10:14:40Z","body":"Oops I just noticed that we're iterating while removing elements from the `HashSet`. For some reason it works but I don't think that it's a good thing to do?\r\n\r\nEdit: The `HashSet` header says:\r\n\r\n```\r\n/**\r\n * Implementation of Set using a bidi indexed hash map.\r\n * Use RBSet instead of this only if the following conditions are met:\r\n *\r\n * - You need to keep an iterator or const pointer to Key and you intend to add/remove elements in the meantime.\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'm afraid I might have ran into undefined behavior indeed, or at least something unpredictable. I'll fix this ASAP.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4066552782/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4066818477","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116513#issuecomment-4066818477","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116513","id":4066818477,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7yZrmt","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-16T10:57:17Z","updated_at":"2026-03-16T10:57:17Z","body":"Should be fixed, but I'm double-checking on my VM with some debug logging to make sure.\r\n\r\nWhile `RBSet` should support this well with the common \"`Element` loop\" idiom, I chose to be double-safe and iterate on a copy of the keys, so that we're completely isolated from whatever happens to the names set. It's a bunch of extra allocations, but the average client receives less than a hundred globals and it's cleanup code.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://ap